 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
- * A fixed 64-sample circle demonstrates native sample rate selection.
- * Its RF offset is Fs/64: changing Fs changes the actual transmitted tone.
+ * IQ lab on the T-Deck: native sample rate + arbitrary tone offset.
+ *
+ * The RF SRAM holds a looped IQ waveform of N samples (N multiple of the
+ * hardware loop alignment, up to max_samples) containing m whole turns of
+ * a circle. The transmitted offset from the channel centre is
+ *
+ *     offset = Fs * m / N
+ *
+ * "tone <Msps> [offset_MHz]" picks the (N, m) pair closest to the request.
+ * Commands come from the USB serial console and from the T-Deck keyboard
+ * (I2C 0x55) typed on the on-screen input line.
  */
 #include <inttypes.h>
